<?xml version="1.1" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog" xmlns:ext="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog-ext" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog-ext http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-ext.xsd http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-3.6.xsd">

    <!--
      The Träger-authored Erstantwort Bausteine and the Antwortfrist
      (ORISO-Admin#601, ADR-018).

      Five text columns, one per Baustein a Träger owns in its own voice: greeting,
      who reads along, the emergency-numbers addition, the single free notice, and
      the closing. Columns rather than a new table because these have exactly the
      lifecycle of the existing content_impressum / content_privacy bodies, and the
      machine-translation-on-publish mechanism is already wired to that shape.

      EXACTLY ONE free notice, enforced by there being one column. ADR-018 §2 makes
      it the single deliberate escape hatch; a collection would have made that a
      validation rule somebody could later relax.

      NO columns for the derived Bausteine (the deadline wording, "send us no
      personal data", the modality note). Those are rendered from configuration, and
      giving them a text field is precisely the failure ADR-018 §2 forbids: a typed
      claim about the system can be false, a rendered one cannot.

      MIGRATION DECISION — no backfill, all nullable. NULL means "this Träger never
      authored anything", which is what the resolution chain
      Fachbereich ?? Beratungsstelle ?? Träger ?? Plattform reads as "ask the level
      below". Writing the platform default into every tenant would make an
      unconfigured tenant indistinguishable from one that deliberately typed the
      same words, and would freeze today's platform wording into every row.

      erstantwort_response_deadline_days is likewise NOT defaulted to the platform's
      2 Werktage. A tenant that never chose stays distinguishable from one that chose
      2 — which matters the day the platform default changes.

      TEXT (not VARCHAR) matches content_impressum: these are rich-text bodies from
      the same editor stack and outgrew VARCHAR once already (changeset 0022).
    -->
    <changeSet author="oriso" id="addErstantwortTexts">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="tenant" columnName="content_erstantwort_greeting"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <sqlFile path="db/changelog/changeset/0028_tenant_erstantwort_texts/addErstantwortTexts.sql" stripComments="true" />
        <rollback>
            <sql>ALTER TABLE `tenantservice`.`tenant` DROP COLUMN `content_erstantwort_greeting`, DROP COLUMN `content_erstantwort_who_reads_along`, DROP COLUMN `content_erstantwort_emergency_addition`, DROP COLUMN `content_erstantwort_free_notice`, DROP COLUMN `content_erstantwort_closing`, DROP COLUMN `erstantwort_response_deadline_days`;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
